From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:22:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MediaError.message is empty when a fallback media engine
 fails after the first

Need the bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

When the media engine that loads a resource fails before metadata,
MediaPlayer::networkStateChanged() records the engine's error message
and then lets the next installed engine try. With the GStreamer ports
that engine is MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamerMSE, which fails any load
without a MediaSource with FormatError and no message, and that empty
message replaced the one from the engine that actually tried to play
the resource. MediaError.message was therefore empty whenever the
GStreamer engine failed to load a progressive resource before metadata.
An error message is now recorded only when the failing engine provides
one.

* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/MediaPlayer.cpp:
(WebCore::MediaPlayer::networkStateChanged):

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/MediaPlayer.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/MediaPlayer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/MediaPlayer.cpp
@@ -1559,8 +1559,11 @@ void MediaPlayer::setPrivateBrowsingMode
 void MediaPlayer::networkStateChanged()
 {
     RefPtr playerPrivate = m_private;
-    if (playerPrivate->networkState() >= MediaPlayer::NetworkState::FormatError)
-        m_lastErrorMessage = playerPrivate->errorMessage();
+    if (playerPrivate->networkState() >= MediaPlayer::NetworkState::FormatError) {
+        // An engine tried after the one that failed may fail without saying why; keep the reason already known.
+        if (auto errorMessage = playerPrivate->errorMessage(); !errorMessage.isEmpty())
+            m_lastErrorMessage = WTF::move(errorMessage);
+    }
     Ref client = this->client();
     // If more than one media engine is installed and this one failed before finding metadata,
     // let the next engine try. Trigger this engine-fallback only for FormatError or DecodeError
